"helpguide.restore.title" = "8. Restore Original JPEG";
"helpguide.restore.intro" = "This does not convert arbitrary images to JPEG. Restoration requires original-JPEG reconstruction data inside the JXL. Lossless image pixels do not imply that the original JPEG data was saved.";
"helpguide.restore.1.title" = "File or folder: restore JPEG files";
"helpguide.restore.1.body" = "The operation extracts JPEG data from reconstructible JXLs without selecting a new quality or applying lossy re-encoding. By default, output goes into a separate _restored_jpeg folder; successfully verified source JXLs are then removed. Unrestorable items are retained and reported. The CLI --keep-source option also retains restored JXLs; the interface currently uses the default behavior.";
"helpguide.restore.2.title" = "Photos library: recovery checks only";
"helpguide.restore.2.body" = "After selecting a Photos library package, check the whole library or a selected album scope. A resource path inside a library also uses this audit, not ordinary file export. The operation creates reports and adds references to items needing attention in MFB JXL Audit albums. It changes album membership, but does not export JPEGs or delete or replace media. A visible photo or thumbnail does not prove that its original resource can be restored. Unavailable resources and missing evidence must remain explicit.";
"helpguide.restore.3.title" = "Exact restoration is not re-encoding";
"helpguide.restore.3.body" = "Output must pass reconstruction-data, current-source identity and applicable XMP checks; a successful decoder exit alone is insufficient. Conflicting XMP inside the JXL and in an adjacent sidecar, or unverifiable output XMP, blocks new output and retains the source and associated files. Conflicting metadata is not written into the original JPEG. Without a saved historical original hash, this is not a historical-hash comparison. A JXL encoded from PNG pixels cannot recreate JPEG original data that was never stored, and the operation does not substitute JPEG re-encoding for restoration.";
"metadata.recovery_collect" = "Copies verified originals from the matching backup. The backup is never changed, and uncertain matches are skipped.";
"metadata.backup_compare" = "Compares two Photos libraries without changing either one.";
